     "answer": "<p>Eigenvalues: a<sub>1</sub> = 1<sup>3</sup> = 1, a<sub>2</sub> = 2<sup>3</sup> = 8. The state as printed is not normalised, so divide by ⟨ψ|ψ⟩.</p><div class=\"worked\"><div class=\"solve\"><div class=\"eq\">⟨ψ|ψ⟩ = |1/√5|<sup>2</sup> + |1/√10|<sup>2</sup> = 1/5 + 1/10 = 3/10</div><div class=\"eq\">⟨ψ|Â|ψ⟩ = 1 × (1/5) + 8 × (1/10) = 0.2 + 0.8 = 1</div><div class=\"eq\">⟨Â⟩ = ⟨ψ|Â|ψ⟩/⟨ψ|ψ⟩ = 1/(3/10)</div></div><div class=\"result\"><p>⟨Â⟩ = 10/3 ≈ 3.33 (probabilities 2/3 for a = 1 and 1/3 for a = 8)</p></div></div><p>If the normalisation is ignored, ⟨ψ|Â|ψ⟩ = 1 is obtained; mention the normalisation step, since 1/5 + 1/10 ≠ 1.</p>"
