    {
     "n": "4a",
     "answer": "<p>The k-th excited state has n = k + 1, so the jump is n = 7 → n = 5.</p><div class=\"worked\"><div class=\"given\"><p>L = 5 × 10<sup>−10</sup> m, m = 9.1 × 10<sup>−31</sup> kg, h = 6.626 × 10<sup>−34</sup> J s</p></div><div class=\"solve\"><div class=\"eq\">ΔE = (7² − 5²) h²/(8mL²) = 24h²/(8mL²) = 3h²/(mL²)</div><div class=\"eq\">ν = ΔE/h = 3h/(mL²) = 3(6.626 × 10<sup>−34</sup>) / [(9.1 × 10<sup>−31</sup>)(25 × 10<sup>−20</sup>)]</div><div class=\"eq\">ν = 1.988 × 10<sup>−33</sup> / 2.275 × 10<sup>−49</sup> = 8.74 × 10<sup>15</sup> Hz</div><div class=\"eq\">ΔE = hν = 5.79 × 10<sup>−18</sup> J ≈ 36.2 eV</div><div class=\"eq\">λ = c/ν = 3 × 10<sup>8</sup> / 8.74 × 10<sup>15</sup> = 3.43 × 10<sup>−8</sup> m</div></div><div class=\"result\"><p>ν ≈ 8.74 × 10<sup>15</sup> Hz, λ ≈ 34.3 nm (far ultraviolet)</p></div></div>"
    },
    {
     "n": "4b",
     "answer": "<p>Along each axis a standing wave fits n half-wavelengths: L = nλ/2, so λ = 2L/n.</p><div class=\"worked\"><div class=\"solve\"><div class=\"eq\">λ<sub>x</sub> = 2L/2 = 2 nm, λ<sub>y</sub> = 2L/1 = 4 nm, λ<sub>z</sub> = 2L/1 = 4 nm</div><div class=\"eq\">E = (h²/8mL²)(n<sub>x</sub>² + n<sub>y</sub>² + n<sub>z</sub>²) = 6h²/(8mL²)</div><div class=\"eq\">h²/(8mL²) = (6.626 × 10<sup>−34</sup>)² / [8(9.1 × 10<sup>−31</sup>)(4 × 10<sup>−18</sup>)] = 4.390 × 10<sup>−67</sup> / 2.912 × 10<sup>−47</sup> = 1.508 × 10<sup>−20</sup> J</div><div class=\"eq\">E = 6 × 1.508 × 10<sup>−20</sup> = 9.05 × 10<sup>−20</sup> J = 9.05 × 10<sup>−20</sup> / 1.6 × 10<sup>−19</sup> eV</div></div><div class=\"result\"><p>λ<sub>x</sub> = 2 nm, λ<sub>y</sub> = λ<sub>z</sub> = 4 nm; E ≈ 0.565 eV</p></div></div><p>This level is 3-fold degenerate: (2,1,1), (1,2,1), (1,1,2) have the same energy.</p>"
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "answer": "<p><b>Derivation.</b> V = 0 for 0 &lt; x &lt; L, infinite outside, so ψ(0) = ψ(L) = 0.</p><div class=\"worked\"><div class=\"solve\"><div class=\"eq\">TISE inside: d²ψ/dx² + k²ψ = 0, k² = 2mE/ℏ²</div><div class=\"eq\">ψ = A sin kx + B cos kx; ψ(0) = 0 ⇒ B = 0</div><div class=\"eq\">ψ(L) = 0 ⇒ kL = nπ, n = 1, 2, 3, …</div><div class=\"eq\">E<sub>n</sub> = n²π²ℏ²/(2mL²) = n²h²/(8mL²), ψ<sub>n</sub> = √(2/L) sin(nπx/L)</div></div><div class=\"result\"><p>E<sub>n</sub> = n²h²/(8mL²)</p></div></div><p><b>Finding L.</b> √E<sub>n</sub> = n · h/(L√(8m)), a straight line through the origin with slope A = h/(L√(8m)).</p><div class=\"worked\"><div class=\"solve\"><div class=\"eq\">A = 0.1 eV<sup>1/2</sup> = 0.1 × (1.6 × 10<sup>−19</sup> J)<sup>1/2</sup> = 0.1 × 4 × 10<sup>−10</sup> = 4 × 10<sup>−11</sup> J<sup>1/2</sup></div><div class=\"eq\">√(8m) = √(8 × 9.1 × 10<sup>−31</sup>) = √(7.28 × 10<sup>−30</sup>) = 2.698 × 10<sup>−15</sup> kg<sup>1/2</sup></div><div class=\"eq\">L = h/(√(8m) A) = 6.626 × 10<sup>−34</sup> / (2.698 × 10<sup>−15</sup> × 4 × 10<sup>−11</sup>) = 6.626 × 10<sup>−34</sup> / 1.079 × 10<sup>−25</sup></div></div><div class=\"result\"><p>L ≈ 6.14 × 10<sup>−9</sup> m = 6.14 nm</p></div></div><p class=\"note\">Check: E<sub>1</sub> = A² = 0.01 eV, and h²/(8mL²) for L = 6.14 nm gives 1.6 × 10<sup>−21</sup> J = 0.01 eV.</p>"
    }
